# 42 MHz on the CORE clock (period 23.809524 ns).
#
# Hardware chain: 27 MHz on D18 -> GTP_PPLL I=1/M=1/F=56/O0=36 -> 27*56/36 = 42.000 MHz.
# VCO = 1512 MHz (legal 1330..2133), PFD = 27 MHz.
#
# Why 42: the redirect cut (docs/patches/redirect-cut.patch) brings the routed worst
# path from 25.43 ns down to 22.68 ns (measured, build P23c at a 45 MHz constraint,
# where it still missed by 0.462 ns).  23.81 ns therefore closes with ~1.1 ns margin
# while staying on the same RTL family that routed in 112-183 rounds.
create_clock -name board_clk -period 37.037037 -waveform {0 18.5185185} [get_ports {clk}]
create_clock -name core_clk -period 23.809524 -waveform {0 11.904762} [get_pins {u_core_pll/CLKOUT0}]
